     "content": "# Result\n\nThe specified one-active-color curved family now has a sharp finite-rank orbital stability interval. For r>=2, a>0 and N_psi=N_chi=N>0, it is stable exactly for 0<kappa<=r*kappa_star(N), with kappa_star/N approximately 0.03760248457. At zero stiffness an unused color drifts in diamond holonomy; above the upper boundary scalar active-color instability embeds. At r=1 the earlier interval includes zero.\n\nOff-diagonal color modes have positive matter stiffness and positive Gauss-reduced mass. Their magnetic Hessian vanishes by the two-color determinant -1 identity. Exact section polynomials of degrees 1,3,2,4,2 specify twenty-eight complex slice oscillators per unused color, independent of kappa. The unused vacuum block supplies positive cycle stiffness for kappa>0. Full nonlinear energy separation preserves the scalar critical quartic. The proof does not assume a smooth final residual U(r-1) quotient.\n\n57 exact constructor checks, full matrix rank-two/rank-three fixtures and two rank-two nonlinear campaigns passed. Independent review and physical bridge work remain open. No action change or empirical data; physical promotion 0.\n\n# Higher-rank curved branch stability v0.1\n\nThe unchanged candidate U(r) action admits the embedded curved orbit U_e=diag(-i b_e,I), E=0, psi=chi=sqrt(N)v e1. For every finite r>=2 it is nonlinearly orbitally stable exactly for 0<kappa<=r*kappa_star(N), where kappa_star/N is approximately 0.03760248457. The scalar r=1 orbit separately retains stability at kappa=0. Unused-color cycle drift proves the higher-rank zero-stiffness exception; above the upper threshold active scalar instability embeds.\n\nEach active-to-unused color has twenty-eight complex positive-frequency oscillators in the linear symplectic slice, with exact pencil degrees 1,3,2,4,2. Their magnetic Hessian is zero and their restoring matter energy is positive. The residual global U(r-1) zero-moment constraint remains imposed; this is not a summed smooth physical mode count. The nonlinear energy proof covers the full fixed-norm surface, including all Gauss-admissible perturbations, and preserves the scalar positive-quartic endpoint.\n\nRead `UD_HIGHER_RANK_CURVED_STABILITY_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf` and its TeX. Run `python3 verify_higher_rank.py` with SymPy, NumPy and SciPy to reproduce 57 exact checks, inherited integer endpoint certification, linear spectrum checks, rank-two/rank-three matrix fixtures and two separately typed full nonlinear rank-two campaigns. Exact color blocks and bases are in `HIGHER_RANK_EXACT_VERIFICATION_v0.1.json`.\n\nIndependent review pending; development lane with no registry entry; unchanged candidate action; no experimental data; physical promotion 0. Earlier artifacts remain frozen.\n"
+  },
